The purpose of this section is teaching:

```text id="xmlns353"
how to FILTER collections of data based on conditions/rules
```

Meaning:

```text id="xmlns354"
go through a collection and keep ONLY the items that match what you want
```

This is one of the MOST common operations in real software engineering.

---

# What You’re Practicing

You are practicing:

* looping through collections
* checking conditions
* selecting matching data
* building filtered results
* conditional collection processing

---

# Core Pattern Being Taught

This pattern:

```ruby id="xmlns355"
new_array = []

collection.each do |item|
  if condition
    new_array << item
  end
end
```

is the foundation of filtering logic.

---

# Simple Example

Your code:

```ruby id="xmlns356"
if item[:price] < 10
```

means:

```text id="xmlns357"
“keep only cheap items”
```

